    "done_when": "Read section 7 of a-worker-cannot-write-your-home first. The fence binds the operator's ~/.codex/auth.json writable into a fenced codex run; the bind is in reckon/_backends.py, near CODEX_AUTH_FILENAME. A fenced run cannot remove it or replace it, by rename over it or by unlink and recreate. A truncation to zero bytes is detected after the run and reported on the run's record and on stderr, not silently persisted. Detection compares the file's size before launch with its size after the run ends; it does not read or print the file's contents. tests/test_fenced_codex_can_persist_its_login.py gains these cases, and every case uses a temporary home, never the operator's real ~/.codex. The removal, replacement and truncation cases each fail at your base or are shown to hold there already, and the manifest says which. The section's evidence half concerns an earlier run's record: leave other runs' records alone and say so in the manifest. Existing fence and codex-login tests keep passing; grep tests/ for auth.json, CODEX_AUTH_FILENAME and the fence's bind helpers to build the gate. Record the outcome in docs/evidence/fragments/a-worker-cannot-write-your-home/codex-login-cannot-be-removed.html. Run `date -u` first and treat that instant as your start; your deadline is 60 minutes later. Write your manifest before starting any long command. Run both gate arms with pytest-xdist (-n 8 --timeout=300), never serially. Run the base arm, from a `git archive` extraction of your base under /tmp in a directory named for this run, and then the head arm, each in the foreground: a background command dies when your turn ends. Keep the gate to the test files that reach your change, tens of files rather than hundreds. Each arm uses its own basetemp outside any repository and writes to its own new log path, which it never overwrites. Each arm is recorded as JSON carrying completed true and a literal command with absolute paths and no angle-bracket placeholder. Each log names its revision on the first line as revision= followed by the full sha, and ends with a bare line reading EXIT= followed by the exit code. The head arm adds no failure id; any added id means status blocked, naming each id. ruff check and ruff format --check over the changed Python paths report no finding the base did not. Scratch goes under /tmp in a directory named for this run and is deleted before status complete. The turn ends once the manifest reads complete or blocked.",
